00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:07.719 align:start position:0%
EU finance ministers meeting in Brussels  approved a political agreement reached  with the European Parliament to  harmonize EU rules on deposit guarantee  schemes protecting savings deposits of  up to 100,000 euro ministers also agreed  on the need to come to a quick agreement  with the European Parliament on the  establishment of a common mechanism for  rescuing failing banks in a drive to  avoid any repetition of taxpayer-funded  bailouts the Hellenic presidency is  committed to do all it can within its  purview to achieve an agreement based on  mutual consensus as the best way to  guarantee the resolution mechanism  effective and efficient operation and we  want every member state to be on board  the Greek presidency will now explore  new ideas to find a compromise which is  acceptable to all parties ministers also  adopted the Commission's third alert  mechanism report which is the starting  point of the e u--'s annual macro  economic imbalance procedure the council  welcomed progress made by member states  in correcting both the external and  internal imbalances but warned that  further progress is needed in relation  to the annual growth survey 2014 the  council shared the Commission's analysis  of the current economic situation and  asks member states to continue growth  friendly fiscal consolidation tackling  unemployment and modernizing public  administration to consolidate the  incipient economic recovery as foreseen  the council adopted a recommendation on  the budget discharge for 2012 and  concluded that next year's budget should  reflect member states whose fiscal  consolidation efforts and fund  investments to boost growth and jobs
 

